---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/config.js";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Disclaimer | CANIX402"
  description="Terms of use and risk disclaimer for the Canix402 x402-gated DeFi opportunities data API on Algorand and Base."
  keywords="Canix402 terms, disclaimer, risk, x402 API"
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Terms &amp; Disclaimer</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">
    Last updated: July 2026. These terms apply to use of the Canix402 API and this
    documentation site.
  </p>

  <div class="prose-section">
    <h2>Informational service only</h2>
    <p>
      Canix402 provides machine-readable DeFi opportunity data for developers and
      autonomous agents. Nothing on this site or returned by the API constitutes
      financial, investment, tax, or legal advice.
    </p>

    <h2>No guarantees on data</h2>
    <p>
      Yield figures (APY, APR), TVL, and related metrics are sourced from third-party
      protocols and normalized for agent consumption. Data may be delayed, incomplete,
      or inaccurate. We do not guarantee correctness, completeness, or timeliness of
      any response.
    </p>

    <h2>Use at your own risk</h2>
    <p>
      You are solely responsible for evaluating data before acting on it, including
      any on-chain transactions your agent or wallet performs. DeFi protocols carry
      smart-contract, liquidity, oracle, and market risks that this API does not
      assess or mitigate.
    </p>

    <h2>x402 payments</h2>
    <p>
      Paid endpoints require USDC micropayments via the x402 protocol. An agent may pay on
      Algorand, on Base, or on both. An Algorand payment is complete without a Base address.
      Payments are processed through third-party facilitators and blockchain networks. Fees paid
      for API access are generally non-refundable. Failed requests due to client
      errors, invalid payment proofs, or upstream unavailability do not entitle you to
      a refund unless required by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      The API aggregates data from independent Algorand DeFi protocols and Morpho on Base, and relies on
      external infrastructure (facilitators, RPC nodes, hosting providers). We are not
      responsible for outages, policy changes, or actions of those third parties.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The API and this site are provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as
      available&rdquo; basis without warranties of any kind, express or implied,
      including merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.operator} and its operators shall
      not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages
      arising from use of the API or reliance on its data, including loss of funds
      or missed opportunities.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update pricing, endpoints, data schemas, or these terms at any time.
      Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms or the service:
      <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
